course: dictionary
lesson: 3674
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. You can find the right one by reading the words around it. Fixed is a good example, because it can mean several different things.
explain: «The broken bike was fixed by the mechanic.» Here fixed means repaired, made to work again. «Its huge eyes are fixed tubes that cannot roll.» Here fixed means attached firmly so it cannot move.
explain: «A liquid has a fixed volume but takes the shape of its container.» Here fixed means set and not changing. To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence. Set and not changing still makes sense, so you have it right.
fact: Fixed can mean repaired, made to work again.
fact: Fixed can mean attached firmly so it cannot move, as in «fixed to the wall».
fact: Fixed can mean set and not changing, as in «a fixed price» or «a fixed time».
fact: Fixed can also mean arranged dishonestly, as in a fixed game or result.
exercise: «The owl's eyes are fixed tubes that cannot roll.» What does fixed mean here? | Set and not changing | Arranged dishonestly | Repaired and working again | *Attached firmly so they cannot move
exercise: «The garage will get my bike fixed by Friday.» What does fixed mean? | Arranged dishonestly | Set and not changing | *Made to work again | Attached to the wall
exercise: Find and copy the word that means set and not changing in this sentence: «A loan means borrowing a set amount and paying it back in fixed amounts plus interest.» | *fixed | amounts | interest | borrowing
test: «She kept a fixed smile all through the long speech.» What does fixed mean here? | Arranged dishonestly | Firmly attached to her face | Repaired and working again | *Not changing
test: «The result of the match was fixed before the game even started.» What does fixed suggest? | *Arranged dishonestly | Repaired | Set in place | Firmly attached
exam: «A lever is a stiff bar that turns round a fixed point called a pivot.» Which meaning fits best? | Happy and smiling | Repaired and working again | Arranged dishonestly | *Set in one place and not moving
